Data Types:-The type of value a variable can store.
It can be divided based oon categories:---
1.Numeric: int(stores the whole numbers can be postive negative or zero(eg:-5)), float(decimal number(eg:-17.7, 7.0), complex(mixed with letter (eg:- 2+3j, 5+7j)
2.Sequence: str("Sujatha"), list([7,17,18]-->it should be ordered and mutubalemeans after creation also we can modified intial state), 
tuple((2,3,4,5)--> it is ordered and immutable means cannot be modified once they are created), range(sequence of numbers(eg:-ragne(5))
3.Set: set(unordered collection of unique items{1,2,3,4,5}, frozenset(Immutable set({1,2,3,4,5.6})
4.Mapping: dict(key-value pairs eg:-{"name":"Sujatha", "age":20}
5.Binary: bytes(Immutable binary data(b"Sujatha") , bytearray(mutable binary data (bytearray(17))
6.Boolean: bool(True(0) or False(1)
7.None: NoneType(represent no value)

